1. The text argues that God is an all-encompassing creative force that creates every possibility, and that suffering and evil are not objective realities but subjective choices made by conscious beings who select their own experiences of reality.

2. I partially agree. The idea that perception shapes our experience of reality is psychologically valid and empowering, as it emphasizes personal agency. However, I disagree with the implication that systemic suffering—such as war, disease, or exploitation—is merely a subjective choice, as this risks dismissing the very real, objective harm inflicted on individuals who do not choose their circumstances.

3. A vessel holds the light,
   Of all that God has made.
   We choose our path through day and night,
   The joys and fears displayed.

   The world may seem a cruel place,
   With pain and evil near,
   But it is but our own embrace,
   Of what we choose to hear.

   For every soul is free to move,
   Through space and through time's stream,
   To find the peace and endless love,
   Of a waking, conscious dream. [end of text]


